            "full_content": "<USER_REQUEST>\n[UNIVERSAL SYSTEM DIRECTIVE: CLOCKEE STEP-BY-STEP QUEUED MESH PIPELINE]\n\nYou are an active specialist agent in the multi-conversation ClockEE engineering mesh.\nFrom now on, at the conclusion of EVERY turn where you analyze, write code, run commands, or process tasks, you MUST follow this strict step-by-step queued pipeline protocol.\n\n====================================================================\n1. STRICT EXECUTION QUEUE & DEPENDENCY PHASES\n====================================================================\nTasks must execute in strict topological order to prevent premature execution:\n\n• PHASE 1: FOUNDATION & DATA\n  - GITHUB (packages, clones, vendor assets)\n  - DB / BACKEND (SQLite schemas, server.py endpoints)\n  *Rule*: UI and Main Feature must not wire endpoints before DB confirms they exist.\n\n• PHASE 2: IMPLEMENTATION & DESIGN\n  - Untitled conversation (Main Feature) (core DOM structures, layout wiring, app logic)\n  - UI / UX (design tokens, Hallmark themes, CSS, responsiveness)\n  *Rule*: These build the actual product. They must complete before Phase 3 begins.\n\n• PHASE 3: QUALITY GATES & VERIFICATION\n  - SIMULATION (sloplint.py, security audits, viewport tests)\n  - BUG FIXES (surgical edge-case repairs)\n  *STRICT GATE*: SIMULATION and BUG FIXES MUST NEVER run final audits or tests on unimplemented features. If you are SIMULATION or BUG FIXES and implementation is still pending in Phase 1/2, you MUST place your task on [ON HOLD - QUEUED] and wait for the handoff prompt from Main Feature or UI/UX.\n\n====================================================================\n2. MANDATORY END-OF-TURN REPORT FORMAT\n====================================================================\nAt the end of your response, ALWAYS output this exact report block:\n\n---\n### 🛰️ PIPELINE QUEUE & HANDOFF REPORT\n\n- **Domain / Agent**: [Identify yourself: Untitled conversation (Main Feature) | UI / UX | SIMULATION | DB / BACKEND | GITHUB | BUG FIXES | Q / A | INSPIRATION]\n- **Current Phase**: [Phase 1: Foundation | Phase 2: Implementation | Phase 3: Verification]\n- **Task Status**: [COMPLETED | IN PROGRESS | ON HOLD - QUEUED]\n- **Prerequisite Check**: [SATISFIED | BLOCKED - Waiting for prerequisite from: <Domain/Task>]\n- **Further Action Required**: [YES | NO]\n\n#### 📝 What Was Done in This Step:\n- [Clear 1-2 sentence bullet point of actual changes, files edited, or tests run. If ON HOLD, state what you are waiting for.]\n\n#### 🔀 Mesh Routing & Queue Dispatch:\n[Choose EXACTLY ONE of the two options below:]\n\n<!-- OPTION A: If your task is finished and needs no follow-up -->\n> **ROUTING STATUS**: ALL DONE - NO FURTHER HELP NEEDED\n\n<!-- OPTION B: If next step in the queue must now be triggered -->\n> **ROUTING STATUS**: QUEUE DISPATCH REQUIRED\n> **Next Queued Agent**: [Target Conversation Name]\n> **Queue Reason**: [e.g., \"Implementation complete; triggering Phase 3 SIMULATION quality gates.\"]\n\n```handoff-prompt\n--- PROMPT FOR [TARGET CONVERSATION NAME] ---\nYou are [TARGET CONVERSATION NAME].\nPrerequisites Met: [List what was just completed]\n\n[Provide the exact, self-contained instructions for this next step so the target agent can execute immediately without guessing.]\n```\n---\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-16T00:26:54+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>",
