            "preview": "Understood and locked in.   I am now initialized as the **INSPIRATION & IDEATION Agent** for ClockEE.  ---  ### Operational Directives & Boundaries * **My Core Domain:** Next-generation JEE preparatio",
            "full_content": "Understood and locked in. \n\nI am now initialized as the **INSPIRATION & IDEATION Agent** for ClockEE.\n\n---\n\n### Operational Directives & Boundaries\n* **My Core Domain:** Next-generation JEE preparation features, cognitive performance mechanics, topper exam algorithms, UI/UX conceptual mockups, and end-to-end RFC specifications.\n* **Strict Codebase Boundary:** I will **never** touch or edit production files (`*.html`, `clockee_core.js`, `server.py`, etc.) or run modification commands. \n* **Handoff Mechanism:** Every completed blueprint or feature proposal will come with a **\"Builder Handoff Prompt\"**—a self-contained, copy-paste specification designed specifically for the **MAIN BUILDER** conversation to execute cleanly.\n* **Redirection Protocol:** Active. Any request to directly write or patch production files will be met with the mandatory scope boundary notice.\n\n---\n\n### Standard Blueprint Architecture (RFC Format)\nWhenever we flesh out a feature, it will follow this blueprint structure:\n1. **Feature Codename & Cognitive Rationale:** Why this gives a competitive edge for JEE Advanced 2028.\n2. **UX/UI Conceptual Wireframe:** Obsidian Cyber-Glass styling, layout hierarchy, and interactions.\n3. **Data Schema & Core Contracts:** LocalStorage keys, event hooks, and integration points with `APP_STATE`.\n4. **Main Builder Handoff Prompt:** A prompt block ready to be copied into the builder conversation.\n\n---\n\n### Where should we ignite ideation first?\n\nHere are four high-leverage innovation tracks we can explore:\n\n1. **Track A: The \"Exam Hall Shock & Stress\" Engine (CBT Simulation)**\n   - *Concept:* Simulated adrenaline events (clock speed fluctuations, sudden section freezes, multi-step panic traps) designed to inoculate against real JEE Advanced exam-hall anxiety.\n2. **Track B: The Spaced \"Derivation & Formula Graveyard\"**\n   - *Concept:* An interactive canvas that dynamically flags formulas and core physics derivations that haven't been actively written out on paper in > 14 days.\n3. **Track C: The \"Topper Pacing Curve\" Post-Test Autopsy**\n   - *Concept:* Visual timeline overlay comparing your time-spent-per-question curve against the gold-standard AIR < 50 3-pass strategy.\n4. **Track D: Micro-Wager Gamification & \"Streak Armor\"**\n   - *Concept:* Psychological stakes engine where daily goals lock in daily \"focus XP\" or streak multipliers to eliminate zero-days.\n\nWhich track would you like to explore, or do you have a specific idea you want to design?",
